{"authored" [{"question" "q-347169" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{5\\pi /3}({cos}^{2}⁡(3x)-4{sin}^{2}⁡(3x))\\,\\text{d}x=$ \n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/state.json" "file_sha256" "c120718f931743c0d70fc46b9969277639e5f9861a4347dee3126eaccbdfe717" "basis" 1134 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-347169" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall  ${cos}^{2}⁡\\theta =1-{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta ,$ so letting $\\theta =3x,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{cos}^{2}⁡(3x)-4{sin}^{2}⁡(3x) & =1-{sin}^{2}⁡(3x)-4{sin}^{2}⁡(3x) \\\\  & =1-5{sin}^{2}⁡(3x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's recall the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${sin}^{2}$ term: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta =1-2{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \n$$\n\nWe can rearrange the above formula as\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{2}(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta )={sin}^{2}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nLetting $\\theta =3x,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{2}(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x))={sin}^{2}⁡(3x).\n$$\n\nWe can now integrate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{5\\pi /3}(1-5{sin}^{2}⁡(3x))\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{5\\pi /3}(1-5\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)))\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{5\\pi /3}(\\frac{5}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)-\\frac{3}{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(\\frac{5}{12}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6x)-\\frac{3}{2}x)\\,|}_{\\pi /3}^{5\\pi /3} \\\\  & =[\\frac{5}{12}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6\\cdot \\frac{5\\pi }{3})-\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot \\frac{5\\pi }{3}]-[\\frac{5}{12}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{3})-\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{3}] \\\\  & =[0-\\frac{5\\pi }{2}]-[0-\\frac{\\pi }{2}] \\\\  & =-2\\pi \\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/state.json" "file_sha256" "c120718f931743c0d70fc46b9969277639e5f9861a4347dee3126eaccbdfe717" "basis" 1134 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-347169" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4630758fe7518876b4078da53f63d140afc115ff54e30376f6c8b26fc3d8c081" "basis" 1134 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-347169" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/state.json" "file_sha256" "c120718f931743c0d70fc46b9969277639e5f9861a4347dee3126eaccbdfe717" "basis" 1134 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-347169" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-2\\pi"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/state.json" "file_sha256" "c120718f931743c0d70fc46b9969277639e5f9861a4347dee3126eaccbdfe717" "basis" 1134 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-74407" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int (3{x}^{2}+10{sin}^{2}⁡5x-10{cos}^{2}⁡5x)\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069587/state.json" "file_sha256" "2983f4fe328c89fa4a840348f8991c022656b5e770733b30137d1c1f70ad373f"} {"question" "q-74407" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Here, we use the double-angle formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta ={cos}^{2}⁡\\theta -{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \n$$\n\nLetting $\\theta =5x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡10x={cos}^{2}⁡5x-{sin}^{2}⁡5x.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (3{x}^{2}+10{sin}^{2}⁡5x-10{cos}^{2}⁡5x)\\text{d}x & =\\int (3{x}^{2}-10({cos}^{2}⁡5x-{sin}^{2}⁡5x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (3{x}^{2}-10\\operatorname{cos}⁡10x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={x}^{3}-10(\\frac{1}{10}\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡10x)+C \\\\  & ={x}^{3}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡10x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069587/state.json" "file_sha256" "2983f4fe328c89fa4a840348f8991c022656b5e770733b30137d1c1f70ad373f"} {"question" "q-74407" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069587/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3f0ef1e2cc5820a983fe85f1772d8da0b5325175b896a35589de81a78df57f06"} {"question" "q-74407" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069587/state.json" "file_sha256" "2983f4fe328c89fa4a840348f8991c022656b5e770733b30137d1c1f70ad373f"} {"question" "q-74407" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "3-\\operatorname{sin}⁡10x+C"] ["math" "{x}^{3}+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡10x+C"] ["math" "{x}^{3}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡10x+C"] ["math" "{x}^{3}-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡10x+C"] ["math" "{x}^{3}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡10x+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069587/state.json" "file_sha256" "2983f4fe328c89fa4a840348f8991c022656b5e770733b30137d1c1f70ad373f"} {"question" "q-74407" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{x}^{3}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡10x+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069587/state.json" "file_sha256" "2983f4fe328c89fa4a840348f8991c022656b5e770733b30137d1c1f70ad373f"} {"question" "q-74408" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate \n$\\int (5-8{cos}^{2}⁡2x)\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069587/state.json" "file_sha256" "2983f4fe328c89fa4a840348f8991c022656b5e770733b30137d1c1f70ad373f"} {"question" "q-74408" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Here, we use the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${cos}^{2}⁡\\theta $ term, given by\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta =2{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta -1.\n$$\n\n \n\nRearranging, we have\n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta +1).\n$$\n\nLetting $\\theta =2x$, we have\n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}⁡2x=\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+1).\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (5-8{cos}^{2}⁡2x)\\text{d}x & =\\int [5-8\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+1)]\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int [5-4(\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+1)]\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (1-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x-4(\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x)+C \\\\  & =x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069587/state.json" "file_sha256" "2983f4fe328c89fa4a840348f8991c022656b5e770733b30137d1c1f70ad373f"} {"question" "q-74408" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069587/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3f0ef1e2cc5820a983fe85f1772d8da0b5325175b896a35589de81a78df57f06"} {"question" "q-74408" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069587/state.json" "file_sha256" "2983f4fe328c89fa4a840348f8991c022656b5e770733b30137d1c1f70ad373f"} {"question" "q-74408" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "5x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+C"] ["math" "5x-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+C"] ["math" "5x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+C"] ["math" "x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+C"] ["math" "x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069587/state.json" "file_sha256" "2983f4fe328c89fa4a840348f8991c022656b5e770733b30137d1c1f70ad373f"} {"question" "q-74408" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+C"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069587/state.json" "file_sha256" "2983f4fe328c89fa4a840348f8991c022656b5e770733b30137d1c1f70ad373f"} {"question" "q-114703" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int ({sin}^{2}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069587/state.json" "file_sha256" "2983f4fe328c89fa4a840348f8991c022656b5e770733b30137d1c1f70ad373f"} {"question" "q-114703" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's recall the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${sin}^{2}$ term: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x=1-2{sin}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nWe can rearrange the above formula as\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{2}(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)={sin}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nWe can now integrate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ({sin}^{2}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{1}{2}(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}x+\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)+C \\\\  & =\\frac{x}{2}+\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069587/state.json" "file_sha256" "2983f4fe328c89fa4a840348f8991c022656b5e770733b30137d1c1f70ad373f"} {"question" "q-114703" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069587/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3f0ef1e2cc5820a983fe85f1772d8da0b5325175b896a35589de81a78df57f06"} {"question" "q-114703" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069587/state.json" "file_sha256" "2983f4fe328c89fa4a840348f8991c022656b5e770733b30137d1c1f70ad373f"} {"question" "q-114703" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{x}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C"] ["math" "2x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C"] ["math" "\\frac{x}{2}+\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C"] ["math" "x+4\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C"] ["math" "x-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069587/state.json" "file_sha256" "2983f4fe328c89fa4a840348f8991c022656b5e770733b30137d1c1f70ad373f"} {"question" "q-114703" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{x}{2}+\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069587/state.json" "file_sha256" "2983f4fe328c89fa4a840348f8991c022656b5e770733b30137d1c1f70ad373f"} {"question" "q-347169" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{5\\pi /3}({cos}^{2}⁡(3x)-4{sin}^{2}⁡(3x))\\,\\text{d}x=$ \n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069587/state.json" "file_sha256" "2983f4fe328c89fa4a840348f8991c022656b5e770733b30137d1c1f70ad373f"} {"question" "q-347169" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall  ${cos}^{2}⁡\\theta =1-{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta ,$ so letting $\\theta =3x,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{cos}^{2}⁡(3x)-4{sin}^{2}⁡(3x) & =1-{sin}^{2}⁡(3x)-4{sin}^{2}⁡(3x) \\\\  & =1-5{sin}^{2}⁡(3x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's recall the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${sin}^{2}$ term: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta =1-2{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \n$$\n\nWe can rearrange the above formula as\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{2}(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta )={sin}^{2}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nLetting $\\theta =3x,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{2}(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x))={sin}^{2}⁡(3x).\n$$\n\nWe can now integrate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{5\\pi /3}(1-5{sin}^{2}⁡(3x))\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{5\\pi /3}(1-5\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)))\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{5\\pi /3}(\\frac{5}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)-\\frac{3}{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(\\frac{5}{12}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6x)-\\frac{3}{2}x)\\,|}_{\\pi /3}^{5\\pi /3} \\\\  & =[\\frac{5}{12}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6\\cdot \\frac{5\\pi }{3})-\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot \\frac{5\\pi }{3}]-[\\frac{5}{12}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{3})-\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{3}] \\\\  & =[0-\\frac{5\\pi }{2}]-[0-\\frac{\\pi }{2}] \\\\  & =-2\\pi \\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069587/state.json" "file_sha256" "2983f4fe328c89fa4a840348f8991c022656b5e770733b30137d1c1f70ad373f"} {"question" "q-347169" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069587/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3f0ef1e2cc5820a983fe85f1772d8da0b5325175b896a35589de81a78df57f06"} {"question" "q-347169" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069587/state.json" "file_sha256" "2983f4fe328c89fa4a840348f8991c022656b5e770733b30137d1c1f70ad373f"} {"question" "q-347169" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-2\\pi"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069587/state.json" "file_sha256" "2983f4fe328c89fa4a840348f8991c022656b5e770733b30137d1c1f70ad373f"} {"question" "q-348755" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069587/assets/e0a3fb0f4fc900f6ef8ac041ded7553f7ac44cc09f946bc3ebfee8a3235e8e94.png)\n\nFind the area $A$ of the region in the $xy$-plane that is bounded by the curve $y=5{cos}^{2}⁡(2x)+2{sin}^{2}⁡(2x)+1,$ the $x$-axis and the lines $x=-\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ and $x=0,$ as shown above. Do not round the answer\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069587/state.json" "file_sha256" "2983f4fe328c89fa4a840348f8991c022656b5e770733b30137d1c1f70ad373f"} {"question" "q-348755" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The area of the region is given by\n\n$$\nA={\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{0}(5{cos}^{2}⁡(2x)+2{sin}^{2}⁡(2x)+1)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nRecall  ${cos}^{2}⁡x+{sin}^{2}⁡x=1,$ so we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5{cos}^{2}⁡(2x)+2{sin}^{2}⁡(2x)+1 & =3{cos}^{2}⁡(2x)+2({sin}^{2}⁡(2x)+{cos}^{2}⁡(2x))+1 \\\\  & =3{cos}^{2}⁡(2x)+3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, we use the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${cos}^{2}⁡x$ term, given by\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x=2{cos}^{2}⁡x-1.\n$$\n\n \n\nRearranging, we have\n\n$$\n2{cos}^{2}⁡x=\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+1.\n$$\n\nHence, the area of the region is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{0}(3{cos}^{2}⁡(2x)+3)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{0}(\\frac{3}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+1)+3)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{0}(\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+\\frac{9}{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(\\frac{3}{8}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+\\frac{9}{2}x)\\,|}_{-\\pi /2}^{0} \\\\  & =(\\frac{3}{8}\\operatorname{sin}⁡0+\\frac{9}{2}\\cdot 0)-(\\frac{3}{8}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-2\\pi )+\\frac{9}{2}\\cdot (-\\frac{\\pi }{2})) \\\\  & =(0+0)-(0-\\frac{9\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{9\\pi }{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069587/state.json" "file_sha256" "2983f4fe328c89fa4a840348f8991c022656b5e770733b30137d1c1f70ad373f"} {"question" "q-348755" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069587/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3f0ef1e2cc5820a983fe85f1772d8da0b5325175b896a35589de81a78df57f06"} {"question" "q-348755" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069587/state.json" "file_sha256" "2983f4fe328c89fa4a840348f8991c022656b5e770733b30137d1c1f70ad373f"} {"question" "q-348755" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{9\\pi}{4}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069587/state.json" "file_sha256" "2983f4fe328c89fa4a840348f8991c022656b5e770733b30137d1c1f70ad373f"}] "usage" {"q-347169" []} "basis" 2382 "retractions" [] "immutable_answers" [17592186288690] "immutable_fields" [[17592186288689 :answer-field/correct] [17592186288689 :answer-field/id] [17592186288689 :answer-field/key] [17592186288689 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
